+<body>
+<div class="wrap">
+  <h1>Er:Al₂O₃ strip-loaded waveguide amplifier</h1>
+  <p class="sub">An erbium-doped Al₂O₃ strip loads a thin film of Al₂O₃, Si₃N₄, LiNbO₃ (TFLN) or LiTaO₃ (TFLT) on SiO₂, with a SiO₂ top cladding or air above. The pump and signal modes are solved for the cross-section, their overlaps with the doped strip feed steady-state erbium rate equations, and the pump and signal are propagated along the device to give the gain spectrum.</p>
+
+  <div class="layout">
+    <aside class="side">
+      <div class="card">
+        <h2>Platform (film under the strip)</h2>
+        <div class="seg" id="platSeg" role="group" aria-label="Film material">
+          <button type="button" data-v="al2o3">Al₂O₃</button>
+          <button type="button" data-v="sin">Si₃N₄</button>
+          <button type="button" data-v="tfln">TFLN</button>
+          <button type="button" data-v="tflt">TFLT</button>
+        </div>
+        <div class="grp">Top cladding (superstrate)</div>
+        <div class="seg" id="supSeg" role="group" aria-label="Top cladding">
+          <button type="button" data-v="sio2">SiO₂ cladding</button>
+          <button type="button" data-v="air">Air (uncladded)</button>
+        </div>
+        <div id="cGeo"></div>
+        <p class="hint">Choosing a platform loads typical dimensions. TFLN and TFLT are taken as x-cut: quasi-TE sees n<sub>e</sub>, quasi-TM sees n<sub>o</sub>.</p>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="card">
+        <h2>Erbium and device</h2>
+        <div id="cEr"></div>
+        <div class="grp">Spectroscopy</div>
+        <div class="seg" id="cupSeg" role="group" aria-label="Upconversion model">
+          <button type="button" data-v="fixed">C<sub>up</sub> fixed</button>
